{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he shall go out to the altar that is before YHWH, etc.</b> The sprinklings that are before the kapporet effect atonement for the impurity of the Sanctuary and its consecrated things — those of the innermost sanctum; and the sprinklings that are upon the parokhet in the Tent of Meeting effect atonement for the impurity of the Hekhal and its consecrated things, such as the menorah, the table, the showbread, and the parokhet itself; and the applications of the inner altar and the sprinklings upon it effect atonement for the impurity of the altar itself and its consecrated things, such as the incense. Therefore Scripture divides them and mentions each atonement separately. And in Torat Kohanim (section 4, chapter 1, halakhah 2) this is derived from the verse at the end (Leviticus 16:20), \"And he shall finish making atonement for the holy,\" etc., and they said: \"making atonement for the holy\" — this refers to the innermost sanctum; \"the Tent of Meeting\" — this is the Hekhal; \"the altar\" — this is the inner altar; this teaches that each one has its own atonement. From here they said: If he applied some of the inner applications and the blood was spilled, he must bring other blood and begin from the beginning with the inner applications. If he completed the inner applications and the blood was spilled, he must bring other blood and begin from the beginning with the outer applications. If he completed the outer applications and the blood was spilled, he must bring other blood and begin from the beginning with the applications of the altar, and so forth."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The phrase 'the outer applications' (מתנות שבחוץ) refers to the sprinklings on the parokhet in the Hekhal, contrasted with those 'inside' (בפנים) the innermost sanctum."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:54:22.326751618Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}